Exact methods, including mixed-integer programming (MIP) and constraint programming (CP),
have been proposed by \cite{ref_mip_1}. However, these methods are typically limited to
small-scale instances due to the NP-hard nature of the problem.

Metaheuristic algorithms have been widely applied to medium and large-scale instances.
Genetic algorithms \cite{ref_ga_1}, simulated annealing \cite{ref_sa_1}, iterated
greedy \cite{ref_ig_1}, tabu search \cite{ref_ts_1}, and memetic algorithms
\cite{ref_ma_1} have shown promising results.

